  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "abb3a3e3-00cf-f5ce-6551-62187b39ccf1",
      "object": "block",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "payment-access-tradeoffs\n\nThe feature as described would give sales reps direct access to individual user payment histories. Transaction amounts, dates, merchant names, categories, recurring patterns, balance changes over time.\n\nWhy this feels wrong:\n- Users signed up for a financial management tool, not a sales intelligence platform\n- Payment history reveals deeply personal information: income, spending habits, financial health, even location patterns from merchant names\n- Sales reps using this to personalize outreach is surveillance disguised as customer service\n- No user consent for this specific use case. Our TOS and privacy policy don't cover it\n\nTrevor sees a competitive advantage. I see a trust violation that could end up on the front page of TechCrunch.\n\nNeed to figure out how to handle this without just saying no and getting fired.",
              "link": null
            },
            "plain_text": "payment-access-tradeoffs\n\nThe feature as described would give sales reps direct access to individual user payment histories. Transaction amounts, dates, merchant names, categories, recurring patterns, balance changes over time.\n\nWhy this feels wrong:\n- Users signed up for a financial management tool, not a sales intelligence platform\n- Payment history reveals deeply personal information: income, spending habits, financial health, even location patterns from merchant names\n- Sales reps using this to personalize outreach is surveillance disguised as customer service\n- No user consent for this specific use case. Our TOS and privacy policy don't cover it\n\nTrevor sees a competitive advantage. I see a trust violation that could end up on the front page of TechCrunch.\n\nNeed to figure out how to handle this without just saying no and getting fired.",
            "href": null,
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "1f19a0f0-0357-944a-c317-d0a99a821e14"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-01-08T15:30:00.000Z",
      "created_by_id": "ca6a6e7a-9cc9-94b0-d147-cf4df0202707",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-01-08T16:15:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_by_id": "ca6a6e7a-9cc9-94b0-d147-cf4df0202707",
      "has_children": false,
      "archived": false,
