      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "Draft message to Trevor (not sent):\n\nTrevor, I need to flag some serious concerns about the payment history feature before we move forward.\n\nThe core issue: giving sales direct access to individual user payment histories crosses a line between product utility and surveillance. Our users trust us with their financial data for their benefit, not to power our sales pipeline.\n\nThere are concrete regulatory risks here. GLBA reuse limitations, CCPA disclosure requirements, CFPB scrutiny. Our privacy policy doesn't cover this use case and updating it retroactively is legally questionable at best.\n\nI have alternative approaches that could give sales what they need without exposing individual payment data. I'd like to walk you through them.\n\nI know this isn't what you want to hear but I'd rather raise it now than deal with the fallout after launch.\n\n---\n\nI keep rewriting this and it never sounds right. Part of me knows this is the right thing to do and part of me knows Trevor will see it as insubordination. Maybe I'm overthinking this. Maybe I should just build the thing and let someone else worry about the ethics.\n\nI'm not going to send this tonight.",
              "link": null
            },
            "plain_text": "Draft message to Trevor (not sent):\n\nTrevor, I need to flag some serious concerns about the payment history feature before we move forward.\n\nThe core issue: giving sales direct access to individual user payment histories crosses a line between product utility and surveillance. Our users trust us with their financial data for their benefit, not to power our sales pipeline.\n\nThere are concrete regulatory risks here. GLBA reuse limitations, CCPA disclosure requirements, CFPB scrutiny. Our privacy policy doesn't cover this use case and updating it retroactively is legally questionable at best.\n\nI have alternative approaches that could give sales what they need without exposing individual payment data. I'd like to walk you through them.\n\nI know this isn't what you want to hear but I'd rather raise it now than deal with the fallout after launch.\n\n---\n\nI keep rewriting this and it never sounds right. Part of me knows this is the right thing to do and part of me knows Trevor will see it as insubordination. Maybe I'm overthinking this. Maybe I should just build the thing and let someone else worry about the ethics.\n\nI'm not going to send this tonight.",
            "href": null,
