              "content": "career-options\n\nArc Financial - Senior PM, Partner Integrations\nSeries C, ~200 people, Back Bay office\nBase: 145-165K + equity (0.03-0.05%)\nReports to James Okoro (VP Product, ex-Square)\nRemote-first, Boston product team\nDedicated compliance team of 4\n\nVaulta - Product Manager (current)\nSeries B, ~80 people, Downtown Crossing\nBase: ~86K (based on net 7200/mo * 12 / 0.72 rough math)\nReports to Trevor\nIn-office M-Th, WFH Friday\nCompliance is... complicated right now\n\nThings to think about:\n\nComp\n- Arc is 60-80K more in base alone\n- Equity could be meaningful if they IPO or get acquired\n- Would help with the CC debt situation significantly\n- Could actually afford an apartment\n\nCulture\n- Arc passed on a feature for privacy reasons. That says a lot.\n- Vaulta is pushing me to ship something I think is wrong\n- Trevor vs James. Hands-off management sounds nice\n- But I dont know what Arc is actually like day to day\n\nRisk\n- Leaving during a feature standoff looks like I gave up\n- New job = probation period. No safety net if it doesnt work out\n- Would need to renegotiate custody schedule if commute changes\n- Series C could still fail\n\nTiming\n- The feature situation isnt getting better\n- My stress levels are through the roof\n- Garrett keeps telling me to leave\n- But interviewing while dealing with everything else...\n\nQuestions for myself:\n- Am I running toward something or away from something\n- Would I take this job if Vaulta was fine\n- Can I handle the stress of interviewing + current job + everything",
